lefield, you may search your library for an Aura card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.", 'When Hero of the Nyxborn enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.\\nWhenever you cast a spell that targets Hero of the Nyxborn, creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'When Heroes of the Revel enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 red Satyr creature token with "This creature can\'t block."\\nWhenever you cast a spell that targets Heroes of the Revel, creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'When Hyrax Tower Scout enters the battlefield, untap target creature.', 'When Irreverent Revelers enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Destroy target artifact.\\n• Irreverent Revelers gains haste until end of turn.', "When Kroxa enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless it escaped.\\nWhenever Kroxa enters the battlefield or attacks, each opponent discards a card, then each opponent who didn't discard a nonland card this way loses 3 life.\\nEscape—{B}{B}{R}{R}, Exile five other cards from your graveyard. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its escape cost.)", 'When Lagonna-Band Storyteller enters the battlefield, you may put target enchantment card from your graveyard on top of your library. If you do, you gain life equal to its mana value.', "When Leonin of the Lost Pride dies, exile target card from an opponent's graveyard.", "When Nylea's Huntmaster enters the battlefield, target creature you control gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is your devotion to green. (Each {G} in the mana costs of permanents you control counts toward your devotion to green.)", 'When Ox of Agonas enters the battlefield, discard your hand, then draw three cards.\\nEscape—{R}{R}, Exile eight other cards from your graveyard. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its escape cost.)\\nOx of Agonas escapes with a +1/+1 counter on it.', "When Pheres-Band Brawler enters the battlefield, it fights up to one target creature you don't control. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)", 'When Rage-Scarred Berserker enters the battlefield, target creature you control gets +1/+0 and gains indestructible until end of turn. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy it.)', 'When Reverent Hoplite enters the battlefield, create a number of 1/1 white Human Soldier creature tokens equal to your devotion to white. (Each {W} in the mana costs of permanents you control counts toward your devotion to white.)', 'When Rumbling Sentry enters the battlefield, scry 1.', 'When Setessan Petitioner enters the battlefield, you gain life equal to your devotion to green. (Each {G} in the mana costs of permanents you control counts toward your devotion to green.)', 'When Siona, Captain of the Pyleas enters the battlefield, look at the top seven cards of your library. You may reveal an Aura card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\\nWhenever an Aura you control becomes attached to a creature you control, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.', "When Soul-Guide Lantern enters the battlefield, exile target card from a graveyard.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Soul-Guide Lantern: Exile each opponent's graveyard.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Soul-Guide Lantern: Draw a card.", "When Thassa's Oracle enters the battlefield, look at the top X cards of your library, where X is your devotion to blue. Put up to one of them on top of your library and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order. If X is greater than or equal to the number of cards in your library, you win the game. (Each {U} in the mana costs of permanents you control counts toward your devotion to blue.)", 'When Treacherous Blessing enters the battlefield, draw three cards.\\nWhenever you cast a spell, you lose 1 life.\\nWhen Treacherous Blessing becomes the target of a spell or ability, sacrifice it.', 'When Uro enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless it escaped.\\nWhenever Uro enters the battlefield or attacks, you gain 3 life and draw a card, then you may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield.\\nEscape—{G}{G}{U}{U}, Exile five other cards from your graveyard. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its escape cost.)', 'When Woe Strider enters the battlefield, create a 0/1 white Goat creature token.\\nSacrifice another creature: Scry 1.\\nEscape—{3}{B}{B}, Exile four other cards from your graveyard. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its escape cost.)\\nWoe Strider escapes with two +1/+1 counters on it.', 'Whenever Tectonic Giant attacks or becomes the target of a spell an opponent controls, choose one —\\n• Tectonic Giant deals 3 damage to each opponent.\\n• Exile the top two cards of your library. Choose one of them. Until the end of your next turn, you may play that card.', 'Whenever Towering-Wave Mystic deals damage, target player mills that many cards.', 'Whenever Underworld Sentinel attacks, exile target creature card from your graveyard.\\nWhen Underworld Sentinel dies, put all cards exiled with it onto the battlefield.', 'Whenever a creature dies, if an Aura you controlled was attached to it, return target creature card with mana value 2 or less from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Whenever a land card is put into your graveyard from anywhere, you gain 1 life.\\n{2}{G}: Mill a card.', 'Whenever an opponent draws a card, Underworld Dreams deals 1 damage to that player.', 'Whenever another creature you control attacks, it gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', "Whenever one or more cards are put into your graveyard from your library, Devourer of Memory gets +1/+1 until end of turn and can't be blocked this turn.\\n{1}{U}{B}: Mill a card.", 'Whenever you cast a spell that targets Hero of the Games, creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever you cast a spell that targets Hero of the Pride, creatures you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.', "Whenever you cast your first spell during each opponent's turn, Dreamstalker Manticore deals 1 damage to any target.", "Whenever you cast your first spell during each opponent's turn, draw a card.", "Whenever you cast your first spell during each opponent's turn, put a +1/+1 counter on Arena Trickster.", "Whenever you cast your first spell during each opponent's turn, you may tap or untap target nonland permanent.", 'Whenever you draw a card, you may pay {1}. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on Nadir Kraken and create a 1/1 blue Tentacle creature token.', 'Whenever you sacrifice a permanent, Slaughter-Priest of Mogis gets +2/+0 until end of turn.\\n{2}, Sacrifice another creature or an enchantment: Slaughter-Priest of Mogis gains first strike until end of turn.', "Whenever you sacrifice a permanent, put a +1/+1 counter on Blood Aspirant.\\n{1}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature or enchantment: Blood Aspirant deals 1 damage to target creature. That creature can't block this turn.", "Wrap in Flames deals 1 damage to each of up to three target creatures. Those creatures can't block this turn.", 'You draw two cards, lose 2 life, then mill two cards.', "You may choose not to untap Entrancing Lyre during your untap step.\\n{X}, {T}: Tap target creature with power X or less. It doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as Entrancing Lyre remains tapped.", 'You may play an additional land on each of your turns.\\nLands you control are every basic land type in addition to their other types.', 'Your devotion to each color and each combination of colors is increased by one.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color. If you control a God, a Demigod, or a legendary enchantment, you gain 1 life.', '[+1]: Create a 2/3 blue and black Nightmare creature token with "Whenever this creature attacks or blocks, each opponent exiles the top two cards of their library."\\n[−3]: Return target nonland permanent to its owner\'s hand, then that player exiles a card from their hand.\\n[−7]: You may cast up to three spells from among face-up cards your opponents own from exile without paying their mana costs.', "[+1]: Look at the top four cards of your library. You may reveal an enchantment card from among them and put that card into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\\n[−3]: Exile target creature or enchantment you don't control until target enchantment you control leaves the battlefield.\\n[−7]: Return all enchantment cards from your graveyard to the battlefield.", '[+2]: Draw a card. Each player mills two cards.\\n[−5]: Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control.\\n[−11]: Gain control of all creatures target opponent controls.', '[+2]: Put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two target creatures.\\n[−2]: Search your library and/or graveyard for a card named Sunlit Hoplite and put it onto the battlefield. If you search your library this way, shuffle.\\n[−8]: Until end of turn, creatures you control gain flying and get +X/+X, where X is your devotion to white.', '[−1]: Up to two target creatures you control each get +2/+1 until end of turn.\\n[−2]: Create two 1/1 white Human Soldier creature tokens.\\n[−3]: You gain 5 life.\\nEscape—{4}{W}{W}, Exile four other cards from your graveyard. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its escape cost.)', "{1}, Sacrifice Traveler's Amulet: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.", '{1}, Sacrifice a creature: Each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', '{1}: Skophos Maze-Warden gets +1/-1 until end of turn.\\nWhenever another creature becomes the target of an ability of a land you control named Labyrinth of Skophos, you may have Skophos Maze-Warden fight that creature. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)', '{1}{R}: Incendiary Oracle gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nIf a creature dealt damage by Incendiary Oracle this turn would die, exile it instead.', '{2}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Draw a card.', '{2}{R}, Discard a card: Draw a card.', '{6}{U}, Sacrifice Eidolon of Philosophy: Draw three cards.', '{G}{W}: Bronzehide Lion gains indestructible until end of turn.\\nWhen Bronzehide Lion dies, return it to the battlefield. It\'s an Aura enchantment with enchant creature you control and "{G}{W}: Enchanted creature gains indestructible until end of turn," and it loses all other abilities.', "{R}, Sacrifice another creature or an enchantment: Skophos Warleader gets +1/+0 and gains menace until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", '{T}: Add one mana of any color. If you control a creature with power 4 or greater, add two mana of any one color instead.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Field of Ruin: Destroy target nonbasic land an opponent controls. Each player searches their library for a basic land card, puts it onto the battlefield, then shuffles.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Remove target attacking or blocking creature from combat.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Spend this mana only to cast artifact spells or activate abilities of artifacts.\\nEquipped creatures you control have flying and haste.']
flavor: ['"A blessing is not a gift. It is a duty."', '"A cyclops thinks slowly but strikes quickly. Try to keep it thinking."\\n—Brigone, soldier of Meletis', '"A great wave crashed, and a mighty wind blew out the stars."\\n—*The Cosmogony*', '"A piercing call, bright as the stars, rang out across the valley, calling the Pheres band to war, to blood and savagery."\\n—Luphea of Setessa, *Histories*', '"Agios was felled by a minotaur\'s blade, but I swear I have seen him since—in the midst of battle, wherever help is needed most."\\n—Phrokos, soldier of Akros', '"And what did Erekastos teach us is the nature of the soul?"', '"As the future slips its way into the present, it ceases to be my concern."', '"As the storm waves crushed my sailors, I cried out to Thassa. The next time I saw them, hard shells encased them, and they swam away to safety."\\n—Siona, captain of the *Pyleas*', '"Be fearless, for a furious rebirth awaits you."\\n—Nylea, god of the hunt', '"Callaphe gazed on the coastline,\\ncertain her destiny called her\\nhere, where the mist-shrouded rocks sang,\\npromising glories undreamed of."\\n—*The Callapheia*', '"Callaphe guided them into the\\ndarkness of Hetos, the bleak mire;\\nBlood-horned minotaurs circled them,\\naxes aglimmer in shadow."\\n—*The Callapheia*', '"Charge bravely. Fight selflessly. Act honorably. Iroas will watch over you."\\n—Verenis, priest of Iroas', '"Cypress leaves for family, larkspur for protection, amaranth for a bountiful harvest."', '"Dawn-kissed, he nourishes the golden grain."\\n—Psemilla, Meletian poet', '"Even in her absence, the light Elspeth kindled in our hearts never faltered."', '"Every dream is a doorway."', '"Everything will be put back in its proper place."\\n—Klothys, god of destiny', '"Evil flourishes where ignorance thrives."\\n—Perisophia the philosopher', '"Far-seeing Kruphix glimpsed the end: Heliod\'s spear cast down and broken."\\n—*The Cosmogony*', '"Feast, for your next meal may be your last!"', '"Flame-wrapped, she dances a burning swath amid the clouds."\\n—Psemilla, Meletian poet', '"For her, I would gladly die again."', '"Freedom lies in accepting a single path."\\n—Nyklos, Meletian philosopher', '"From the ashes of last night\'s revel, I bring the dawn of new growth."', '"Gazing at the unicorn, I felt closer to the majesty of Nyx than I ever had before."\\n—Oineus, traveling merchant', '"Gleams like moonlight on water drew us through the storm and toward our doom."\\n—Siona, captain of the *Pyleas*', '"Grief-struck, she weeps for each mortal\'s final death."\\n—Psemilla, Meletian poet', '"How many more will die before you accept your fate?"\\n—Erebos, god of the dead', '"I bring a dawn that no night can follow."', '"I bring a death none can escape."', '"I bring a fire to recast all the world."', '"I bring a flood that nothing can withstand."', '"I bring a wilderness no law can tame."', '"I don\'t know if the gods watch over their temples, but I figure it\'s best to be stealthy just in case."', '"I like to think Kytheon keeps watch over all of us."', '"I see destruction, suffering, and one tormented glimmer of hope."', '"I see... elk? And lion? And... teeth! A lot of teeth!"\\n—Teraklos of Meletis', '"If you will not pour your drink out for me, I shall pour mine out for you."', '"In every one of you I see a hero\'s heart."', '"It\'s not enough to surprise your opponent. You have to delight the crowd as well."', '"Kroxa devours what he may—not for sustenance or pleasure, but because it is his nature. He is unending hunger given form."\\n—Klothys, god of destiny', '"Many have sought my weakness. All have failed."', '"Many have sought snake-twined Pharika\'s panacea. Do you wish to share their fate?"', '"May the skies be clear of gales and gulls."\\n—Meletian prayer', '"Mogis is pleased by this offering. Bring him more!"', '"My time will come, when all the world will be reforged in the fires of my invention."', '"My time will come, when every soul will bask in my glory and obey my law."', '"My time will come, when life\'s frantic striving will fade into the boundless quiet of death."', '"My time will come, when no road will divide the endless verdure of the trees."', '"My time will come, when the rising tide will surge above the tallest mountain."', '"No power is too great to be undone."\\n—Karametra, god of harvests', '"No, no, and ... no."', '"Not even death can catch me now!"', '"Once you see past the veil we call \'reality,\' altering your own shape is elementary."', '"One-eyed and frightful, the cyclops\\nlifted a boulder and hurled it\\nseaward from cliff\'s edge, shattering\\nmasts and scattering sailors."\\n—*The Callapheia*', '"Only cowards flee from the truth."\\n—Perisophia the philosopher', '"Our stories are full of ancient wisdom; they tell us who we are."', '"Put down your bows, you fools! Arrows only make it angry!"\\n—Callia, Hyrax Tower scout', '"Renata launched a dozen arrows into the minotaur\'s thick hide, but the monster didn\'t slow its charge. The fury of Mogis was upon it."\\n—Luphea of Setessa, *Histories*', '"Renata was mesmerized by the satyr\'s dance of gleeful indifference, of reckless grace and bright disaster."\\n—Luphea of Setessa, *Histories*', '"Right now, in these first moments of creation, it is simultaneously nothing and everything."', '"Sing, beauty. Sing for death, and for the dead."\\n—Ashiok', '"Some aspire to be mighty like the lion or the hydra. I am the parasite that feeds on them all."', '"Storm-tossed and broken, Callaphe cried out to deep-dwelling Thassa.\\nTritons came swiftly to save her, bringing her north to the Lindus."\\n—*The Callapheia*', '"Storms drove them westward to Ketaphos; wide plains shimmered in starlight.\\nCentaurs greeted them, offering gold-hued apples and grain-cakes."\\n—*The Callapheia*', '"Strength, skill, rage—all have their limits, but patience can be infinite."', '"Take your place among the stars."\\n—Kruphix, god of horizons', '"The archon fell like a star from the sky, meeting the rising sun at the horizon\'s edge."\\n—*The Cosmogony*', '"The first griffins were made by the gods to capture falling stars; they were given the keenest eyes and the swiftest wings, and sent to keep watch above the clouds."\\n—*The Cosmogony*', '"The first rule of politics can be learned from a lowly hornbeetle: it is wise to cultivate powerful friends."\\n—Pythamon, sage of Meletis', '"The promise of victory fills my heart. There is no room for fear."', '"The time has come for us to throw off the chains of tyrannical gods and antiquated superstitions."\\n—Tikaia, disciple of Uremides', '"There\'s no success like excess!"', '"To provoke the mountain is to invite the avalanche."\\n—Perisophia the philosopher', '"Tree-tall giants confronted her, fiercely demanding her tribute;\\nFox-cunning Callaphe\'s slippery speaking entangled their senses..."\\n—*The Callapheia*', '"Vine-wreathed, he nurtures life among the dead."\\n—Psemilla, Meletian poet', '"Wave-borne, he watches over secrets of the shore."\\n—Psemilla, Meletian poet', '"We are bearers of the ancient light, keepers of sun-crowned Heliod\'s blessings. Fight, and the light will protect you!"', '"We offer to Mogis the blood of the weak, and in return he makes us strong."', '"Why would I ever want to look away?"', '"You are loved, child."', '"You can no more stop me than you can halt the tide."', '"Zeal is the sharpest blade, and piety the strongest shield."', 'A hero dies, and a legend arises.', 'A sip of recollection, an ocean of regrets.', "A typhon's escape from the Underworld makes armies flee and kingdoms fall.", 'A vision of home, and a glimpse of hope.', 'A weapon of darkness for a warrior of light.', 'Alythos sat and stared blankly out over the glassy oceans of Nerono, trying in vain to remember what he knew he had forgotten.', "An arrow from Nylea's bow never fails to find its mark.", 'An infinite journey in an infinitesimal time.', 'Ancient yet ever-young, it is wise and subtle—and cruel and reckless as the spring itself.', 'As a mortal, Phenax was the first to escape the Underworld. As a god, he brings his pawns along the same dark path.', "Ashiok's minions plumb the depths of the ocean and the psyche.", 'Bassara, the tower of the fox, houses the elite skirmishers who guard the Nessian Wood against trespassers.', 'Brashness is close enough to bravery.', 'Bright flames quell the darkest nightmares.', 'Calix was patient, steadily following Elspeth until their destined confrontation.', 'Caught between life and death, between land and sea, between thought and oblivion.', 'Chosen by Heliod, Daxos approached the pegasus without fear, and rode it without saddle or reins.', 'Cities offer tribute to Ephara and carve her image into their walls, imploring her to protect them from the dangers of the wild.', "Dalakos's invention worked . . . until it didn't.", 'Death turned admirable conviction into pointless intransigence.', 'Deathbellow Canyon echoes with the roars of minotaurs calling each other to battle.', 'Deathless soldiers called phylaskia guard the borders of the Underworld.', 'Desecrating the dead is a convenient way for harpies to expand their foul collections.', "Distant thunder rumbled, a dread forewarning of Keranos's displeasure.", 'Dreams are just one more form of torment.', 'Even in their mountain fortresses, the Akroans have learned not to anger Thassa.', 'Every footstep is a prayer, every road a temple.', 'Every soldier has a place to stand and a role to play.', "Every strike of the smith's hammer infuses a sword with the determination of its creator.", 'For centuries, the minotaur polis of Skophos was unknown to humans. It remains unexplored.', 'From the echoes of a violent life, a terrible foe is born.', 'Funerary masks help the newly dead resist the erosion of memory and identity in the Underworld.', 'Harpies are among the most detested creatures in all of Theros... and they thoroughly deserve it.', 'Hatred is a potent ally, but an insatiable master.', 'Her paean is the clash of spears, her prayer a battle cry.', 'Her webs, spun from her own hair, reach from Nyx to the mortal world and even into the Underworld.', 'Heroic deeds inspire new heroes.', 'His imagination soars from the depths of the sea to the heights of the heavens.', 'In bleak Tizerus, all hope crumbles in your grasp.', 'In the heart of Setessa, the warriors of Leina Tower defend the polis and train its daughters.', 'In times of conflict, the philosophers of Meletis trade their podiums for conveyances of war.', "Instead of performing their daily devotions, Heliod's acolytes spent the morning picking strands of kelp off the altar.", 'Is there a greater promise than the glory of the sunrise?', 'It eats the things that eat the things that are drawn to the light.', 'It slips silently through the still waters of the Labyrinth of Memories to feed.', 'It swims upon the winds and soars through the waves.', "It's a small step from revel to bloodbath.", "It's hard to keep a satyr down, even in the Underworld.", 'Its strings are wayward threads of fate.', 'Klothys set out to mend the destiny of Theros, her fury guiding every stitch.', 'Leonin band together in the Underworld, taking solace in their strength until, at last, both pride and self are forgotten.', 'Leonin fight for neither god nor polis; their loyalty is to their pride.', "Magic is the true artist's medium.", "Meletian mages can't claim the title of thaumaturge until they have received a gift or omen from the gods. Ephara likes to give tangible tokens of her favor.", "Mirinthes thought death was seconds away when the giant's fist closed around him. Two days later, he was praying for death's release.", 'Mogis can fan a small flame of resentment into an inferno of madness.', 'Nature is stillness and savagery in equal measure.', 'Normally, a cerberus sleeps one head at a time.', "Not even death can quench a hero's inner fire.", 'Nylea appeared amid the howl of a hundred beasts.', 'Nylea speaks to her in the windblown leaves; Thassa in the rushing tides.', 'Nylea watches over all the creatures of the forest except for the snakes. Blessed by Pharika, they can take care of themselves.', 'One spiny tree with bitter fruit grows in the realm of Tizerus, outside the palace of Erebos.', 'Phenax is generous with gifts and unforgiving of debts.', "Purphoros forged the manticore's tail from bronze, its teeth from silver, and its heart from hate.", 'Rage-crowned Mogis swiftly rewards the virtue of brutality.', 'Renata led the best hunters in all of Theros on a quest to bring down the terror of the Setessan wilds.', 'Riddles draw you in, paradoxes hold you fast, and answers shatter your perceptions.', 'Some curiosities are best left alone.', 'Starfish are its favorite prey.', "Thassa's favor followed him to the Underworld. Even the waves of Nerono obeyed his will.", 'The Champion reached for a stone, and Heliod placed the sun into her hand.\\n—*The Theriad*', 'The Nessian Wood is never without defenders.', 'The Returned retain no memory of their identities, but sometimes they mindlessly attempt familiar tasks.', 'The Summer Nexus is a holy grove in Setessa where the starfields of Nyx glitter in the shadows.', 'The Underworld erodes memory, identity, and eventually the physical form, leaving only crumbling statues called misera—hollow monuments to mortal futility.', 'The Underworld is anything but a resting place.', 'The best healers are intimately familiar with death.', 'The blessing is not the strength itself, but the knowledge of how to use it.', 'The death of the party.', 'The flamespeakers of Akros live passionately, devoted to Purphoros and the cycle of destructive creation.', 'The forge of Purphoros burns in the heart of Mount Velus, attracting dragons with its blistering heat.', 'The fury of the slaughter god Mogis burns within him.', 'The god of destiny grants her followers vision deeper than sight.', 'The greatest minds in Meletis study under the masters at the Dekatia, a renowned school of magic and philosophy.', 'The light of hope blinded Pantor to the ills of the world.', 'The minotaur polis of Skophos boasts grand temples to the god of slaughter.', 'The more you struggle against death, the tighter its grip becomes.', 'The oracles of Meletis foresaw neither its rise from the depths nor the destruction it would leave in its wake.', 'The scouts of Hyrax Tower keep watch at the edge of Setessan territory, protecting the polis from inhuman monsters and enemy armies.', "The sharp memory of Daxos's death stabbed into Elspeth's soul.", 'The wisdom of the past is written on the bones of ancients.', 'Those caught attempting to escape the Underworld spend the rest of their existence trapped in the Mire of Punishment.', 'Those who die as heroes are permitted to dwell in Ilysia, a protected realm of the Underworld as tranquil and vibrant as the rest is bleak.', 'Those who do not learn from their mistakes are bound to relive them.', 'Those who fought without honor in life are taken to Agonas and doomed to fight forever in its arenas.', 'Those whose lives were uninspired are doomed to the wretched tedium of Phylias in death.', 'Three sharp barks announce an attempt to escape the Underworld. Three sharp bites end it.', 'To a satyr, a stampede is just another kind of revelry.', 'To some satyrs, only blasphemy is sacred.', 'To tame a griffin is to ride into legend.', 'Tritons search for omens in its wake.', "Tycthis's military career was a flop.", 'When memory is torment, oblivion is bliss.', 'When the gods go to war, mortals pay the highest price.', 'Where its feet tread, the thunder of many others will follow.', 'Wherever it walks, famine follows behind.', 'Winners of the Iroan Games are forever remembered as heroes of their people.']
artist: ['Aaron Miller', 'Adam Paquette', 'Alayna Danner', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Andrea Radeck', 'Antonio José Manzanedo', 'Bastien L. Deharme', 'Bayard Wu', 'Billy Christian', 'Bram Sels', 'Brian Valeza', 'Caio Monteiro', 'Campbell White', 'Caroline Gariba', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Ostrowski', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Chris Seaman', 'Christopher Burdett', 'Chuck Lukacs', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Deruchenko Alexander', 'Dmitry Burmak', 'Ekaterina Burmak', 'Emrah Elmasli', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Evyn Fong', 'Filip Burburan', 'Greg Staples', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'Jakub Kasper', 'James Ryman', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Felix', 'Jason Rainville', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jinho Bae', 'Johann Bodin', 'Johannes Voss', 'John Severin Brassell', 'John Stanko', 'John Thacker', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Josh Hass', 'Jung Park', 'Kari Christensen', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lie Setiawan', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Livia Prima', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Marco Teixeira', 'Mark Behm', 'Mark Zug', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Stewart', 'Micah Epstein', 'Michele Parisi', 'Mike Bierek', 'Mike Sass', 'Milivoj Ćeran', 'Noah Bradley', 'PINDURSKI', 'Paul Scott Canavan', 'Piotr Dura', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Sam Burley', 'Sam Rowan', 'Sara Winters', 'Scott Murphy', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Sidharth Chaturvedi', 'Simon Dominic', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Tyler Walpole', 'Uriah Voth', 'Victor Adame Minguez', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Willian Murai', 'Winona Nelson', 'Wisnu Tan', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yigit Koroglu', 'Yongjae Choi', 'Zack Stella', 'Zezhou Chen', 'Zoltan Boros']
